From 0b1b0c9d8e2f4a6b8c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wb <wb@local>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8192cd: swap 8197F HAL sheet to stock WF2409E vintages

The donor GPL bundle predates the shipped WF2409E firmware: stock loads
its RadioA/RadioB/AGC_TAB/MAC_REG/PHY_REG sheets from a later
8197G-sheet vintage ("//rtl8197f version = 69" radio files, 29.6 KB
PHY_REG, firmware header 0x8199 v3) while the donor tree ships 0-vintage
947-byte RadioA with active RXFE writes stock explicitly comments out.
Mechanical byte-exact replacement from the stock kernel carve, donor
symbol names and VAR_MAPPING linkage kept:

- data_RadioA_8197F   947 -> 2178 bytes (v0 -> v69)
- data_RadioB_8197F   608 -> 1500 bytes (v0 -> v69)
- data_AGC_TAB_8197F 4383 -> 1166 bytes (0xc78 Pin=-110dBm schema -> LUT schema)
- data_MAC_REG_8197F 2428 -> 2289 bytes (same RL6302 v018 header, body drift)
- data_PHY_REG_8197F 10688 -> 29625 bytes (v1 PA blocks -> bare 0x1d0c style)
- data_rtl8197Ffw   56080 -> 57272 bytes (0x8197 v8 -> 0x8199 v3)

MAX_CONFIG_FILE_SIZE: stock size-checks parsed files up to 1 MiB and its
PHY_REG sheet alone is 29.6 KB; the donor parser sticks to a 20 KB branch
(8814-family only gets 64 KB). Extend the 64 KB branch to
CONFIG_WLAN_HAL_8197F so the v1 PHY_REG sheet parses whole.

Deliberately not swapped here: PHY_REG_PG_8197Fmp{,_Type0} (stock uses a
different offset family, 0x3a00.. JAGUAR3 codewords vs the donor legacy
0xe00.. rows that the donor set_power_by_rate switch stores; swapping
content alone would drop every row) and TXPWR_LMT (no donor file).

Signed-off-by: Sohan Ali <96324905+sohan-f@users.noreply.github.com>
---
